<title>ISRAEL: Israel's Agan Q4 EPS $0.16 v $0.24.</title>
<headline>Israel's Agan Q4 EPS $0.16 v $0.24.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Agan Chemical</p>
<p>Manufacturers Ltd.</p>
<p>			   (in millions of dollars except EPS)</p>
<p>			  Q4 96     Q4 95	FY 96	FY 95</p>
<p>Revenues		57.7	42.1	 253.2	209.6</p>
<p>Operating profit     4.0	 1.2	  29.8	 25.3</p>
<p>Net Profit	     2.4	 3.6	  23.3	 22.9</p>
<p>Earnings per share  0.16	0.24	  1.55	 1.51</p>
<p>Agan noted that fourth-quarter net earnings were boosted by one-time income of $4.0 million.</p>
<p>Gross margins were slightly higher in the 1996 quarter, at 23.8 percent versus 23.2  percent a year earlier. Operating margins grew to 6.9 percent from 2.8 percent.</p>
<p>Agan said most of last year's revenues growth came from overseas. Sales to overseas markets grew 22.3 percent to $234.6 million while domestic sales grew five percent to $18.6 million.</p>
<p>In the final quarter, revenues grew a faster 37.2 percent because of the inclusion of Agan's newly acquired overseas affiliates in its results. They accounted for 28.3 percent of quarterly sales, Agan said.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
